    "idea": "Passive freed-footprint reuse on strong22, without reserving any free space or requesting expansion.",
    "hypothesis": "Revisit cached addresses of actually freed same-size pipes inside currently verified free physical spans. Parent physical exact fits take priority. A valid cached footprint may choose another containing span or an interior address; stale entries are removed lazily. This differs from earlier rejected exact-slot-growth: never append or reserve capacity while any physical fit exists. It is inspired by donor66 but does not transplant its dual physical/available indices. No measured gain yet.",
    "causality": "Only past frees and current gap containment are used. Every chosen footprint is proved wholly free by current freeByStart. The full parent free pool remains exposed; no slot protection or extra section requests. Metadata erased/split through original parent index helpers. Ordinary large mode only; protected structural routes and all small-population behavior unchanged. Explicit query/hit/stale/changed/interior counters. Source diff and bounds reviewed; strict C++20 Wall/Wextra/Werror syntax passed. Same full15+30development checker and5s/256MiB resource gates.",
